WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.067
The agent platform.

2
00:00:02.367 --> 00:00:06.404
This is the system that differentiates teams in twenty twenty six.

3
00:00:06.404 --> 00:00:07.933
Here is the core insight.

4
00:00:09.133 --> 00:00:10.967
Say this out loud in an interview.

5
00:00:11.267 --> 00:00:14.333
Deterministic code decides what happens next.

6
00:00:14.633 --> 00:00:17.967
The model only makes the judgment calls inside that structure.

7
00:00:19.167 --> 00:00:20.900
The runtime is a state graph.

8
00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:23.900
Plan, act and reflect are explicit nodes.

9
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:27.233
Conditional edges decide whether to loop or finish.

10
00:00:27.533 --> 00:00:32.300
A checkpointer saves state, so runs survive restarts and can pause for a human.

11
00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:35.533
Around that core sit four shells.

12
00:00:35.833 --> 00:00:36.798
First, tools.

13
00:00:36.798 --> 00:00:43.033
Every internal system is wrapped once as an MCP server, reusable and testable alone.

14
00:00:43.333 --> 00:00:44.667
Memory carries state.

15
00:00:44.967 --> 00:00:47.833
Human gates require approval for risky actions.

16
00:00:48.133 --> 00:00:49.867
And tracing logs every step.

17
00:00:51.067 --> 00:00:53.067
Three more controls make it deployable.

18
00:00:53.367 --> 00:00:57.300
Code runs only in a sandbox, with no production credentials.

19
00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:00.516
Budget caps limit iterations, tokens and cost.

20
00:01:00.516 --> 00:01:04.067
That is the difference between an agent and an incident.

21
00:01:04.367 --> 00:01:07.667
And trajectory evals measure logged runs, not vibes.

22
00:01:08.867 --> 00:01:10.567
Here is what interviewers probe.

23
00:01:10.867 --> 00:01:12.433
Start with a single agent.

24
00:01:12.733 --> 00:01:18.200
Split only when one context measurably fails, because coordination overhead is real.

25
00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:22.567
Also remember: everything a tool returns is untrusted input.

26
00:01:22.567 --> 00:01:24.600
That is the injection surface.

27
00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:27.433
Consider failure recovery.

28
00:01:27.733 --> 00:01:30.367
Retries with error feedback beat silent failure.

29
00:01:30.667 --> 00:01:32.800
After a set number of failures, stop.

30
00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:36.733
Then escalate to a human, with the full trajectory attached.

31
00:01:37.933 --> 00:01:38.712
Let's recap.

32
00:01:38.712 --> 00:01:41.567
Code owns the flow, the model owns judgment.

33
00:01:41.867 --> 00:01:44.033
The core is a checkpointed state graph.

34
00:01:44.333 --> 00:01:48.800
Wrap tools in MCP, sandbox execution, and cap budgets.

35
00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:52.130
Start with one agent and gate risky actions.

36
00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:54.333
Next up: Serving and Cost Stack.
